WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. (Take 
whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! Are 
gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.310
Major?

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.790
I hear you took on her Guardians.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.470
News travels fast.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:54.090
Anyway, I saved the real fight for later.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.050
How will you report this?

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.410
My orders from the Baroness 
were to report to her

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:03.080
regardless of the success 
or failure of the mission.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:09.060
Anyway, it's not as if they can escape 
from this continent of Dustvin.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:11.700
I think this goes without saying,

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.180
but any personal feelings 
are strictly off-limits.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.900
What's the matter?

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.530
Why tell me that, Major?

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.070
Turning the "poison which will destroy the 
world" into one of the dearly departed...

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:24.760
That's the only thing I have on my mind.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:37.550
"March of the Half-Baked Knight"

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.530
Whoa!

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.780
Hello there, little lady.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:05.330
Hello.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:06.740
And how are we today?

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.540
Fine, thanks!

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.040
Shannon, some bandits are here.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:12.540
Okay.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.000
What's the matter?

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.500
Bandits, looks like.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.050
Oh.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:21.550
Little lady, do you have something 
nice to share with us?

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:25.800
How about some pickles?

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.770
You're a sweet kid, little lady.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.120
Let's see...

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.860
You! The young man over there!

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:37.780
Yeah?

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:42.110
Leaving all your stuff here and walking 
away is in your own best interest.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.280
Same goes for you.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.410
Look, boy, don't come crying 
to me if you get hurt.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.290
You down there!

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:57.800
I won't tolerate wicked behavior that 
threatens the livelihood of others!

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:02.590
In the stead of Mauser, I 
shall pass judgment over you!

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:04.300
Have at you! Charge!

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.520
Whoa!

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.350
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.150
Stop! Stop!

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.540
Stop! Stop! Whoa!

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:22.860
What was all that about?

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.700
Hey, was he with...

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.750
Y-You little bastard!

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:39.460
Did you make sure it was dry 
before you took it down?

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:42.420
A princess only wears dry clothes.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.930
It'll dry while you're wearing it.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.390
Hang up the stuff that's not 
dry yet inside the wagon.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:50.140
That'll stink it up in here!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.600
Then I won't wear it.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.200
Fine, suit yourself.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.520
In the first place, you...

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:55.390
Huh?

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.980
Are you okay over there?

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:08.200
Yes, I'm fine!

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.780
Well, take care, then!

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.330
Thanks, I will!

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:14.830
H-Hey, wait!

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.830
I noticed that you were in a 
spot of trouble back there.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.550
Oh, that. We're all fine.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:22.660
Are you injured?

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:23.790
Not a scratch!

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.390
Um... Where are you headed now?

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:29.600
Um, well... I thought we'd 
go to some city somewhere.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.720
Oh, so you're on a journey?

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:33.100
Um, sort of.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:36.450
Um, I... Allow me to 
accompany you until then!

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.100
Huh? Well...

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:43.400
Just for a while! Won't you join me 
for a leisurely conversation for a...

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.450
Are you really okay?

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:49.810
Hello?

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.270
Are you okay?

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:02.960
W... Wi... Will...

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:03.590
"Will"?

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:07.360
Will you be my girlfriend, working on the 
assumption that we will marry one day?

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:10.830
What's that you're saying out of the blue?

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:13.100
What do you mean? I'm proposing, of course!

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:16.290
Who <i>are </i>you?

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.770
I'm sorry, where are my manners?

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:21.060
I am Leopold Skorpus,

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:25.140
eldest son of Baron Skorpus, 
lord of the barony of Takos.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:27.360
You're a long way from home, aren't you?

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:30.400
I am on a knight-errantry tour.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:33.030
I hope to gain entry into the Amber Knights.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:36.660
The Amber Knights? You mean 
the order of court knights?

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:37.870
Yes, that's them!

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.670
The elite order of Leinwan Royal Cavaliers?

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.210
Yes, yes! That's exactly right!

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.670
The knights with the most 
powerful armed forces?

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.880
Yes! That's them, all right!

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:52.390
So, are you fine people on a trip?

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.390
Well, something like that.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.400
I understand.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.270
Abandoning a young maiden

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.150
with whom I exchanged marriage 
vows in this lawless zone

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:10.400
would disgrace the name of House 
Skorpus unto its last generation!

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.390
"Exchanged vows with"?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.910
Until we reach the end of this 
highway, allow me to protect you.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:17.330
No thanks.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.540
Now, now, think nothing of it.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:20.830
I said, no thanks.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:22.180
Why not?

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:25.240
He's a little strange, but 
he seems like a fun guy.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.800
Come, then! Let us be off!

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.260
"Pacifica"... What a fine name.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:34.660
Truly, a name worthy of your beauty.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:39.270
Hear that? People with 
a trained eye can tell.

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:41.340
Hear me, Mauser!

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:43.600
I give thanks for this encounter!

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.310
The thing is, Leopold...

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.020
Please, call me Leo.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:50.780
Okay, Leo. What do you do 
on a knight-errantry tour?

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.530
Have you heard the name Doyle Barrett?

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:58.040
As I recall, he was second in command 
of the Amber Knights, wasn't he?

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:03.500
I wish to ask him to tell 
me tales of chivalry.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:06.500
Doing a little networking to get 
in through the back door, huh?

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:10.010
Please don't view everything so cynically.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:12.160
Hear that?

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:16.010
Sir Barrett retired quite 
suddenly fifteen years ago.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:22.270
One theory suggests that he was involved 
with the sealing of the Scrapped Princess.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:26.440
Something about his health being ruined 
from being cursed by the Scrapped Princess.

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:28.020
C-Cursed?!

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.480
It's merely a rumor.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:35.170
I'm not so sure that this "Scrapped 
Princess" ever really existed in the first place.

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:37.530
Hm? Is something the matter?

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:40.690
Um, uh... Nothing at all!

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:47.750
How dazzling...

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:01.890
Your beauty is blinding, Miss Pacifica...

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.440
Oh, I didn't see you there, big brother.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.790
Big brother?

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:11.030
Tell me something...

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:14.440
What do you like about 
that stray cat of a girl?

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:15.740
Everything.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.450
"Everything" doesn't tell me much...

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:21.370
Isn't that how love at first 
sight is supposed to be?

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:22.290
Really?

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.990
If I had to give a reason,

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:27.510
I suppose it would be her dignity.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:30.690
I would hardly call her a <i>stray </i>cat,

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:34.840
but don't you think she has a sort 
of catlike resolute air about her?

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:38.180
In your younger sister, I sense the fortitude

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:41.480
of the great ancient nobility that 
is not to be found in commoners.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:48.480
What are you two up to?

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:52.020
C'mon! Come swimming with me!

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:53.690
Um, I really shouldn't...

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:54.690
What?

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:55.740
Well, I'd rather not.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.320
You can't swim!

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.820
Big brother!

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.790
Nobles and commoners, huh?

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:12.590
Why don't you get cleaned up, too, Shannon?

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:13.390
Sure...

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:16.970
Leo went to all that trouble 
of proposing, but now...

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:20.470
C'mon, now! One, two! One, two!

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:20.470
And he's already turning into her pet.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:28.230
Shannon... Why don't we go 
see this "Doyle" man, too?

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:31.650
All we know about what 
happened fifteen years ago

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:35.070
is what was written in Father's will, right?

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:38.240
This person might know something more.

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:41.700
Please, wait!

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:45.270
You're fine! You're fine! The important 
thing is to get used to the water!

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.460
Take this!

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:51.860
And this!

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:51.860
Miss Pacifica, look!

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:56.200
What is she doing?

00:10:57.830 --> 00:10:59.860
Hello there!

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:02.040
I think she means that something is out here.

00:11:02.820 --> 00:11:07.310
Ma'am! Is there something out here?!

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.390
Curse you, amphibian!

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:44.930
Ow!

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.640
What do you think you're doing 
to the guardian spirit?!

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:50.680
Pacifica!

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:52.240
Would you like a hand?

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:56.080
Are you from around here?

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:57.690
What the heck <i>is </i>that thing?

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:01.030
I believe it is what thy 
kind calls a "dragon."

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.030
A dragon? <i>That</i>?

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:06.830
She must be substituting the genetic 
information of a frog for its basic morphology.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:13.460
This ID signal, it's serial 
seven... It's you, Gloria?

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:18.000
I'm amazed that you're still 
functional in that state...

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.140
I must protect...

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:33.600
I am to protect the world 
that person loved...

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:36.650
Even if it takes thousands, 
tens of thousands, of years.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.280
Pacifica Cassul.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:44.110
Please, make her go to sleep.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:47.660
Just tell her one thing. Just 
tell her, "That's enough."

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:50.490
With our kind, unless 
we are ordered to do so,

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.750
we are unable to even go to sleep on our own.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:55.670
I beg you.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.170
Um...

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.200
Um, look...

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:07.180
That's enough.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:10.930
You can rest now.

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:18.790
Thank you...

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:30.280
Pacifica!

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:32.290
Who are you?

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:34.660
What just happened?

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:37.190
At the moment, you wouldn't 
understand even if I told you.

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:45.460
What in the world was that?

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:47.260
That's what I'd like to know.

00:13:48.150 --> 00:13:51.350
What did you people do 
to the guardian spirit?!

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:54.770
I just said that she could rest now.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:13:59.770
Oh, I see...

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.270
So, the guardian spirit is at rest now...

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.820
Are you folks on a trip?

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:06.690
Yes.

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:09.360
What brings you out to these parts?

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:12.280
We're looking for a man by 
the name of Doyle Barrett.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.290
Huh? Are you sure?

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:19.500
We want to meet this great 
knight ourselves, too.

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:22.500
Doyle... What was it?

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:26.090
Sir Doyle Barrett. Formerly 
of the Royal Cavaliers.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.970
Royal Cavaliers? Oh, <i>him</i>...

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:32.470
She says that there is a mansion here.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:36.470
I say, isn't this exciting?

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:38.040
Not exactly...

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:44.770
Hey, what do we do if he 
really is under a curse?

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:47.070
Do you have powers like that?

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.400
Well, no...

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.770
Maybe it's really true.

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:52.910
Maybe you turn people all fat and bloated.

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:54.490
I'm gonna belt you!

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.000
Shall we go?

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.000
Well, we're off!

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.000
See you soon!

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.790
That's an amazing mansion, all right...

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.790
Hurry up and say something.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:08.420
R-Right.

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:15.560
Can I help you?

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:19.390
Are you... Sir Barrett?

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:20.350
Yes, that's right.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:26.270
M-My goal is to join the Amber Knights!

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:30.700
To that end, I wish to ask you to 
teach me the meaning of chivalry!

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:31.450
Chivalry?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:32.950
Yes, sir!

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:35.950
Then you wasted a trip.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.290
I'm a simple town doctor now.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:44.330
If you've got time enough to 
go searching for that nonsense,

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:45.960
go plow a field or something.

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:49.440
Hey, what's that supposed to mean?!

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:51.590
Leo's idolized you his whole life! And you...

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.670
I never asked for that.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:56.720
I'll have to ask you to leave.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:00.890
Oh, now I get it!

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.640
So, that's the kind of man he is!

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.480
That's too bad, Leo!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:09.530
Boy, worrying that he was fat was 
such a waste of time! Let's go!

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:10.490
Miss Pacifica?

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:13.530
We're going back. What are you waiting for?

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:14.930
Um, there's a...

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:15.900
A what?

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.490
A cliff over there.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.870
Well, that should do the trick.

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:23.830
Thanks.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.940
Now, would you please go away?

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:34.590
I heard stories about you from 
my parents my whole life.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:38.040
That you were a magnificent knight

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:40.600
who knew the true meaning of justice.g

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:44.480
That you understood chivalry 
more clearly than any other man.

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:49.370
Boy, have you ever killed anyone?

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:52.150
A person who didn't resist?

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:54.610
No, sir, I...

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:57.620
Try to kill someone, and you'll understand.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:01.830
Kill someone that you don't 
hate or even dislike.

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:03.370
With your own two hands,

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:05.360
kill someone who's powerless.

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:06.120
Then you'll understand.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:10.250
The whole notion of chivalry is a sham.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:13.740
In this world, there's no such 
thing as absolute right and wrong.

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:15.000
But...

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:17.970
Tell me, boy, what is chivalry?

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.450
What is justice?

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:24.980
I don't know. Will you tell me?

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.430
Go home.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:33.990
I'll come again.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:45.000
Welcome back!

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:48.500
We're back...

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:55.420
Want some?

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.220
I think I'll have some of these eggs...

00:17:58.220 --> 00:17:59.840
Go on, dig in.

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:02.220
It's the least I can do for 
you for appeasing the spirit.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:05.220
Thanks, but I don't think 
we had much to do with it.

00:18:05.220 --> 00:18:08.930
There's an oral tradition that 
says that the guardian spirit

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:12.440
was suffering under a curse 
from the Dark Lord Browning.

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:16.440
I wanted to do something to help her.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:20.070
So maybe I really did give 
her a helping hand...

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.200
Didn't you say that she thanked you?

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:22.950
Yeah...

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:26.010
Then I'm sure that what 
you did was a good deed.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:30.460
Yeah, you're right.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:34.960
By the way, did you folks find Doyle?

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:39.470
We met him, all right, but...

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:44.510
Well, I got the impression that he 
didn't want to talk about knights.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:46.310
Oh, really?

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:49.690
I guess that's because he gave up being 
a knight after something bad happened.

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:52.690
What do you mean?

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:58.740
This was fifteen years ago, back at the 
time of the Revelation of Saint Grendel.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:01.240
They say that the princess 
who had just been born

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:05.700
was born under a star of ill omen.

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:08.250
They said something about 
a sickness or curse.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:11.170
That she was the Scrapped Princess.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:16.880
That man was charged with the 
duty of disposing of the baby.

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:21.480
But apparently, she hardly seemed 
like an abomination at all.

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:24.340
She was just a sweet little baby.

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:42.740
Of course, some rumors say 
that she was secretly spared,

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:47.030
and she's still alive somewhere.

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:50.020
Old woman, that's enough.

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:53.370
Oh, did I ramble on for too long?

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:56.530
Well, there's always a reason for everything.

00:19:56.530 --> 00:19:59.680
So you go easy on him, all right?

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:19.080
Guess who!

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.490
Why the long face?

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:36.530
All I... All I want is to 
become a full-fledged knight.

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.570
To become one of the Amber Knights

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:41.420
and protect the people of the kingdom.

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:44.050
That's all I want.

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:47.510
Miss Pacifica...

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:50.930
What do you suppose chivalry is?

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets 
sail. (The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:46.380
"Next Time"

00:22:34.220 --> 00:22:37.370
The Cassuls get rooms at an 
inn in the town of Taurus.

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:40.630
Pacifica tries to befriend 
a girl who works at the inn,

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:43.170
but the girl doesn't open up to her at all.

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:45.320
She must be the shy type, huh?

00:22:45.320 --> 00:22:47.330
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:47.330 --> 00:22:49.250
"Fanfare for the Unforgiven Man."

00:22:49.250 --> 00:22:50.470
Please tune in!
